{"Denial cache key collision when name or parent contain underscores - userPermDenialCacheKey joins action, name, and parent with underscore separator, causing different (name, parent) pairs like (dash_1, fold) and (dash, 1_fold) to produce identical cache keys, leading to incorrect denial of access to different resources": 0.8629642724990845, "Stale denial cache blocks freshly granted permissions for 30 seconds - the denial cache short-circuits all downstream logic including the new fall-through to DB pattern, so when a user is denied access and then granted permission, the cached denial prevents access until TTL expires": 0.8501052856445312, "No mechanism to invalidate denial cache entries when permissions change - expiry is solely TTL-driven": 0.759510338306427}